# One-shot versus shared live UI

**Prerequisites:** [commands and live tutorial](/docs/tutorials/commands-and-live/).
**Kind:** concept.
**Next:** [Update the UI](/docs/how-to/update-the-ui/).

**One-shot `@patch`:** the acting tab morphs. A second tab stays stale until it
clicks or reloads. That is the correct default (the [counter](/examples/counter/)).

**Shared `@live`:** generated `GET /sse` polls; unchanged HTML is skipped.
Every open tab morphs the region. Use it when two clients must see the same
HTML without a full reload (the [live counter](/examples/live-counter/)).

Cost: an extra route, poll traffic, and conflict rules (`@view("/sse")` is
illegal beside `@live`). Prefer one-shot until a second tab is a real
requirement.

**Related:** [Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).
